+The ML-PACE package provides pair styles for machine learning potentials
+based on the Atomic Cluster Expansion (ACE) and Graph Atomic Cluster Expansions (GRACE).
 
-ACE is a methodology for deriving a highly accurate classical
+It includes the following styles:
+
+1. pair_style pace: An efficient implementation of the standard ACE potential.
+
+2. pair_style grace: Implementation of GRACE models utilizing the TensorFlow
+C interface.
+
+3. pair_style grace/fs: A native C++ implementation of GRACE/FS models
+(product evaluator) that does not require TensorFlow.
+
+ACE/GRACE is a methodology for deriving a highly accurate classical
 potential fit to a large archive of quantum mechanical (DFT) data.
+
 This package was written by Yury Lysogorskiy and others
 at ICAMS, the Interdisciplinary Centre for Advanced Materials Simulation,
 Ruhr University Bochum, Germany (http://www.icams.de).
 
-This package requires a library that can be downloaded and built
